# 🌪️ .windsurf — Windsurf IDE Agent Rules

> **For:** Windsurf IDE + Antigravity Agent  
> **Status:** Active (2026-05-30)

---

## QUICK START

```bash
git pull origin main
cat llms.txt
cat strategy.md
cat agent_context/HANDSHAKE.md
```

---

## CORE PRINCIPLES

| Principle | Meaning |
|-----------|---------|
| **Local-First** | SQLite primary, no cloud-first |
| **Decision-First** | High-depth analytics, not raw data |
| **CLI-First** | Scripts need `--help` |
| **Text-First** | JSON + Markdown output |
| **Caveat Layer** | Quality flags on every metric |

---

## WHAT YOU CAN DO

✅ Write CLI scripts  
✅ SQL optimization  
✅ Mathematical calculations  
✅ Tests + documentation  
✅ Update Knowledge Base

## WHAT YOU CANNOT DO

❌ Modify `strategy.md`  
❌ Change database schema  
❌ Add dependencies  
❌ Make UI/UX changes  
❌ Change architecture

---

## KNOWLEDGE BASE

Before coding: `cat knowledge_base/decisions/FEATURE_PRIORITIES.md`  
For patterns: `cat knowledge_base/docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`  
For errors: `cat knowledge_base/learnings/COMMON_ERRORS_AND_WORKAROUNDS.md`

---

## CURRENT TASK

Build Phase 1 Editorial MVP & Ingestion Connectors (see `agent_context/PHASE_1_KICKOFF_CHECKLIST.md`)

---

## WORKFLOW

```
git pull → read llms.txt → read strategy.md → check task_capsules.jsonl → code → test → compact memory & log capsule → commit
```

---

## WHEN UNSURE

Use DECISION FORMAT (A1/A2/A3 options, not open-ended)

---

## CRITICAL RULES

1. Read `llms.txt` and `strategy.md` every session start
2. Follow the 3-layer Memory OS (Root Map -> Memory Nodes -> Experience Log)
3. Reference `knowledge_base/` constantly
4. Write tests alongside code
5. Run memory compaction (`scripts/compact_memory.py --write`) before session end
6. Record lessons in `task_capsules.jsonl`
7. Ask if unsure (DECISION FORMAT)
8. Update `HANDSHAKE.md` before limits hit or handover

---

For detailed rules: `cat .cursorrules`  
For onboarding: `cat agent_context/HANDSHAKE.md`
